WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:05.299
OK, so that about does it for our introduction to Lightning inside Unreal Engine 5.

2
00:00:05.299 --> 00:00:09.019
We covered a lot of topics in this, so thank you for sticking around for it.

3
00:00:09.019 --> 00:00:12.259
We first took a look at some Lightning terminology as well as the light types that

4
00:00:12.259 --> 00:00:13.859
are available in Unreal.

5
00:00:13.859 --> 00:00:17.500
Then we had a bit of a deep dive into what Lumen is and how you can use it,

6
00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:22.100
as well as how it works in conjunction with Nanite and virtual shadow maps.

7
00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:27.940
We then took a look at the static Lightning solution that we have in Unreal Engine 5,

8
00:00:27.940 --> 00:00:33.179
which is light maps, as well as all the other things that are connected to it,

9
00:00:33.179 --> 00:00:39.310
including reflections, IES profiles, visualization modes.

10
00:00:39.310 --> 00:00:44.950
And yeah, I really hope that you had a good time and that this was informative to you.

11
00:00:44.950 --> 00:00:46.990
Hope to see you in the next one.
